# Checked witnesses for refined Ree two profiles

The tables give representatives and conjugators for a partition of each of the
four original candidate groups. They also list commuting elements for each
order-four representative. Kernel reduction checks the conjugation equations,
the commuting equations, the cardinalities, and the final two fiber tallies.
The tables need not assert that different parts are nonconjugate: the matching
cardinality bounds in `centralizer_card_bounds` establish the centralizer sizes.

The witness search used the collected multiplication of `Core` and the root
conventions of Shinoda (1975), (2.3), pp. 81–82. Every entry used in the proof
is checked against `countMul`, which is proved equal to Sylow multiplication.
-/

